IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb4-common`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part XV, ss 191 and 192: REORGANIZATION AND
-- ARRANGEMENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. Two ways a court can restructure a corporation. A "reorganization" (s 191) is a
-- court order made under the oppression remedy (s 241), the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act or another
-- federal Act; the court may amend the articles, authorize debt and appoint directors. An "arrangement"
-- (s 192) is a fundamental change a solvent corporation puts to the court because it cannot practicably
-- make it under another provision of the Act; the court approves it on such terms as it thinks fit.
-- Section 241 and the sections on certificates (262) belong to piece cb5.

§§ `s 191 Reorganization`

-- src:2433 | Definition of reorganization
-- src:2434 | 191 (1) In this section, reorganization means a court order made under
-- src:2435 | (a) section 241;
-- src:2436 | (b) the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act approving a proposal; or
-- src:2437 | (c) any other Act of Parliament that affects the rights among the corporation, its shareholders and creditors.
@ref CBCA s 191(1) (src:2434-2437)
DECLARE `Kind of court order for s 191(1)` IS ONE OF
    `an order made under section 241`
    `an order under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act approving a proposal`
    `an order under any other Act of Parliament that affects the rights among the corporation, its shareholders and creditors`
    `an order that is none of these`

@ref CBCA s 191(1) (src:2434-2437)
GIVEN order IS A `Kind of court order for s 191(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the order is a reorganization within s 191(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `an order made under section 241` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an order under the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act approving a proposal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an order under any other Act of Parliament that affects the rights among the corporation, its shareholders and creditors` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:2438 | Powers of court
-- src:2439 | (2) If a corporation is subject to an order referred to in subsection (1), its articles may be amended by such order to effect any change that might lawfully be made by an amendment under section 173.
@ref CBCA s 191(2) (src:2439)
GIVEN `the corporation is subject to an order referred to in subsection 191(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is one that might lawfully be made by an amendment under section 173` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the order may amend the articles to effect the change within s 191(2)` MEANS
        `the corporation is subject to an order referred to in subsection 191(1)`
    AND `the change is one that might lawfully be made by an amendment under section 173`

-- src:2440 | Further powers
-- src:2441 | (3) If a court makes an order referred to in subsection (1), the court may also
-- src:2442 | (a) authorize the issue of debt obligations of the corporation, whether or not convertible into shares of any class or having attached any rights or options to acquire shares of any class, and fix the terms thereof; and
-- src:2443 | (b) appoint directors in place of or in addition to all or any of the directors then in office.
@ref CBCA s 191(3)(a) (src:2442)
GIVEN `a court has made an order referred to in subsection 191(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may authorize the issue of debt obligations and fix their terms within s 191(3)(a)` MEANS
    `a court has made an order referred to in subsection 191(1)`

@ref CBCA s 191(3)(b) (src:2443)
GIVEN `a court has made an order referred to in subsection 191(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may appoint directors in place of or in addition to those in office within s 191(3)(b)` MEANS
    `a court has made an order referred to in subsection 191(1)`

-- (4): the duty to send articles of reorganization once an order has been made, with the documents of
-- sections 19 and 113 "if applicable" (pieces cb1 and cb2): not applicable counts as satisfied.
-- src:2444 | Articles of reorganization
-- src:2445 | (4) After an order referred to in subsection (1) has been made, articles of reorganization in the form that the Director fixes shall be sent to the Director together with the documents required by sections 19 and 113, if applicable.
@ref CBCA s 191(4) (src:2445)
GIVEN `an order referred to in subsection 191(1) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must send articles of reorganization to the Director within s 191(4)` MEANS
    `an order referred to in subsection 191(1) has been made`

@ref CBCA s 191(4) (src:2445)
GIVEN `the articles of reorganization are in the form the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: sections 19 and 113 (pieces cb1 and cb2)
      `the documents of sections 19 and 113 are applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents of sections 19 and 113 are sent with them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles of reorganization have been sent as s 191(4) requires` MEANS
        `the articles of reorganization are in the form the Director fixes`
    AND (    (NOT `the documents of sections 19 and 113 are applicable`)
         OR  `the documents of sections 19 and 113 are sent with them`)

-- src:2446 | Certificate of reorganization
-- src:2447 | (5) On receipt of articles of reorganization, the Director shall issue a certificate of amendment in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 191(5) (src:2447)
GIVEN `the Director has received articles of reorganization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a certificate of amendment within s 191(5)` MEANS
    `the Director has received articles of reorganization`

-- src:2448 | Effect of certificate
-- src:2449 | (6) A reorganization becomes effective on the date shown in the certificate of amendment and the articles of incorporation are amended accordingly.
@ref CBCA s 191(6) (src:2449)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the reorganization is effective and the articles are amended on a day within s 191(6)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the date shown in the certificate of amendment`

-- src:2450 | No dissent
-- src:2451 | (7) A shareholder is not entitled to dissent under section 190 if an amendment to the articles of incorporation is effected under this section.
@ref CBCA s 191(7) (src:2451)
GIVEN `an amendment to the articles of incorporation is effected under section 191` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a shareholder is not entitled to dissent under section 190 within s 191(7)` MEANS
    `an amendment to the articles of incorporation is effected under section 191`

§§ `s 192 Arrangement`

-- (1): "arrangement INCLUDES" -- the list is not closed. A transaction on the list is an arrangement; for
-- one that is not on it the subsection does not say (NOTHING), and is not "no".
-- src:2452 | Definition of arrangement
-- src:2453 | 192 (1) In this section, arrangement includes
-- src:2454 | (a) an amendment to the articles of a corporation;
-- src:2455 | (b) an amalgamation of two or more corporations;
-- src:2456 | (c) an amalgamation of a body corporate with a corporation that results in an amalgamated corporation subject to this Act;
-- src:2457 | (d) a division of the business carried on by a corporation;
-- src:2458 | (e) a transfer of all or substantially all the property of a corporation to another body corporate in exchange for property, money or securities of the body corporate;
-- src:2459 | (f) an exchange of securities of a corporation for property, money or other securities of the corporation or property, money or securities of another body corporate;
-- src:2460 | (f.1) a going-private transaction or a squeeze-out transaction in relation to a corporation;
-- src:2461 | (g) a liquidation and dissolution of a corporation; and
-- src:2462 | (h) any combination of the foregoing.
@ref CBCA s 192(1) (src:2453-2462)
DECLARE `Kind of transaction named in s 192(1)` IS ONE OF
    `an amendment to the articles of a corporation (s 192(1)(a))`
    `an amalgamation of two or more corporations (s 192(1)(b))`
    `an amalgamation of a body corporate with a corporation that results in an amalgamated corporation subject to this Act (s 192(1)(c))`
    `a division of the business carried on by a corporation (s 192(1)(d))`
    `a transfer of all or substantially all the property of a corporation to another body corporate in exchange for property, money or securities of the body corporate (s 192(1)(e))`
    `an exchange of securities of a corporation for property, money or other securities of the corporation or property, money or securities of another body corporate (s 192(1)(f))`
    `a going-private transaction or a squeeze-out transaction in relation to a corporation (s 192(1)(f.1))`
    `a liquidation and dissolution of a corporation (s 192(1)(g))`
    `any combination of the foregoing (s 192(1)(h))`
    `a transaction that is not named in s 192(1)`

@ref CBCA s 192(1) (src:2453-2462)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of transaction named in s 192(1)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`whether the transaction is an arrangement within s 192(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a transaction that is not named in s 192(1)` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2): insolvent. Limb (b) counts the stated capital of ALL classes as a liability; section 190(26)(b)
-- does not (see the register).
-- src:2463 | Where corporation insolvent
-- src:2464 | (2) For the purposes of this section, a corporation is insolvent
-- src:2465 | (a) where it is unable to pay its liabilities as they become due; or
-- src:2466 | (b) where the realizable value of the assets of the corporation are less than the aggregate of its liabilities and stated capital of all classes.
@ref CBCA s 192(2) (src:2464-2466)
GIVEN `the corporation is unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the realizable value of the corporation's assets` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of its liabilities` IS A NUMBER
      `the stated capital of all classes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is insolvent within s 192(2)` MEANS
        `the corporation is unable to pay its liabilities as they become due`
    OR  `the realizable value of the corporation's assets` LESS THAN (`the aggregate of its liabilities` PLUS `the stated capital of all classes`)

-- src:2467 | Application to court for approval of arrangement
-- src:2468 | (3) Where it is not practicable for a corporation that is not insolvent to effect a fundamental change in the nature of an arrangement under any other provision of this Act, the corporation may apply to a court for an order approving an arrangement proposed by the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 192(3) (src:2468)
GIVEN `the corporation is insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is not practicable to effect the fundamental change under any other provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may apply to a court for an order approving an arrangement within s 192(3)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation is insolvent`)
    AND `it is not practicable to effect the fundamental change under any other provision of this Act`

-- (4): "any interim or final order it thinks fit including": every order, if the court thinks it fit. The
-- one carve-out the text makes is in paragraph (a): notice may be dispensed with for "any person other
-- than the Director".
-- src:2469 | Powers of court
-- src:2470 | (4) In connection with an application under this section, the court may make any interim or final order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:2471 | (a) an order determining the notice to be given to any interested person or dispensing with notice to any person other than the Director;
-- src:2472 | (b) an order appointing counsel, at the expense of the corporation, to represent the interests of the shareholders;
-- src:2473 | (c) an order requiring a corporation to call, hold and conduct a meeting of holders of securities or options or rights to acquire securities in such manner as the court directs;
-- src:2474 | (d) an order permitting a shareholder to dissent under section 190; and
-- src:2475 | (e) an order approving an arrangement as proposed by the corporation or as amended in any manner the court may direct.
@ref CBCA s 192(4) (src:2470-2475)
DECLARE `Kind of order under s 192(4)` IS ONE OF
    `an order determining the notice to be given to any interested person, or dispensing with notice to a person other than the Director (s 192(4)(a))`
    `an order dispensing with notice to the Director`
    `an order appointing counsel, at the expense of the corporation, to represent the interests of the shareholders (s 192(4)(b))`
    `an order requiring the corporation to call, hold and conduct a meeting of holders of securities or options or rights in the manner the court directs (s 192(4)(c))`
    `an order permitting a shareholder to dissent under section 190 (s 192(4)(d))`
    `an order approving the arrangement as proposed or as amended in a manner the court directs (s 192(4)(e))`
    `any other interim or final order the court thinks fit`

@ref CBCA s 192(4) (src:2470-2475)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 192` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks the order fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A `Kind of order under s 192(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may make the order within s 192(4)` MEANS
        `an application has been made under section 192`
    AND `the court thinks the order fit`
    AND (CONSIDER order
         WHEN `an order dispensing with notice to the Director` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- src:2476 | Notice to Director
-- src:2477 | (5) An applicant for any interim or final order under this section shall give the Director notice of the application and the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 192(5) (src:2477)
GIVEN `the person has applied for an interim or final order under section 192` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the applicant must give the Director notice of the application within s 192(5)` MEANS
    `the person has applied for an interim or final order under section 192`

@ref CBCA s 192(5) (src:2477)
GIVEN `the person has applied for an interim or final order under section 192` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel within s 192(5)` MEANS
    `the person has applied for an interim or final order under section 192`

-- src:2478 | Articles of arrangement
-- src:2479 | (6) After an order referred to in paragraph (4)(e) has been made, articles of arrangement in the form that the Director fixes shall be sent to the Director together with the documents required by sections 19 and 113, if applicable.
@ref CBCA s 192(6) (src:2479)
GIVEN `an order referred to in paragraph 192(4)(e) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must send articles of arrangement to the Director within s 192(6)` MEANS
    `an order referred to in paragraph 192(4)(e) has been made`

@ref CBCA s 192(6) (src:2479)
GIVEN `the articles of arrangement are in the form the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: sections 19 and 113 (pieces cb1 and cb2)
      `the documents of sections 19 and 113 are applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents of sections 19 and 113 are sent with them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles of arrangement have been sent as s 192(6) requires` MEANS
        `the articles of arrangement are in the form the Director fixes`
    AND (    (NOT `the documents of sections 19 and 113 are applicable`)
         OR  `the documents of sections 19 and 113 are sent with them`)

-- src:2480 | Certificate of arrangement
-- src:2481 | (7) On receipt of articles of arrangement, the Director shall issue a certificate of arrangement in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 192(7) (src:2481)
GIVEN `the Director has received articles of arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a certificate of arrangement within s 192(7)` MEANS
    `the Director has received articles of arrangement`

-- src:2482 | Effect of certificate
-- src:2483 | (8) An arrangement becomes effective on the date shown in the certificate of arrangement.
@ref CBCA s 192(8) (src:2483)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of arrangement` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the arrangement is effective on a day within s 192(8)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the date shown in the certificate of arrangement`
